      "Review MSP documentation coverage with a sample drawn from the queue export before the meeting, so the discussion cannot drift to memorable cases. A short written rule is easier to test than an unwritten habit. Keep the prior procedure available for comparison. Set the next review date before the action begins. For MSP documentation coverage, compare the request record with the destination value rather than relying on a status label. Outsourced Billing Services keeps the MSP documentation coverage source, reviewer, and decision date together in the claim file so a later check does not depend on memory.",
      "## Review and next action",
      "The MSP documentation coverage working paper should show the request, the source, the decision, the action, and the surviving value without a private inbox. Keep the source reference and the coded value in the same row. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. Write the note so a reviewer can reconstruct the decision without a meeting. The MSP documentation coverage record should let a second reviewer rebuild the decision from the source document and the reviewer note. For this MSP documentation coverage case, Outsourced Billing Services asks the billing specialist to write the open question and the named approver before the claim moves.",
      "## Sources and review limits",
      "The sources below describe the billing, privacy, and recordkeeping context for this protocol, not a result for this sample. The review compares [the non-covered service workflow](/blog/check-a-non-covered-service-notice-against-the-claim-record) and [the capitation review](/blog/track-a-claim-appeal-through-the-payer-portal-response-file) with this measurement. Each reference is checked against the publisher page on the observation date and kept beside the working file. Findings remain local operational evidence and do not replace a coding, compliance, or contract review. See [CMS: Medicare Claims Processing Manual](https://www.cms.gov/regulations-and-guidance/guidance/manuals/internet-only-manuals-ioms-items/cms018912), [CMS: National Correct Coding Initiative](https://www.cms.gov/medicare/coding-billing/national-correct-coding-initiative-ncci-edits), and [GAO Green Book](https://www.gao.gov/products/gao-14-704g) for the governing context."
